          <div class="note__art"><svg viewBox="0 0 380 240" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="380" height="240" fill="#0C1D30"/><rect x="60" y="86" width="260" height="56" rx="5" fill="#13283E" stroke="#14BDC7" stroke-width="2"/><g fill="#14BDC7"><rect x="80" y="102" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><rect x="108" y="102" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><rect x="136" y="102" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><rect x="164" y="102" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><rect x="192" y="102" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><rect x="220" y="102" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/></g><g fill="#F5A623"><circle cx="90" cy="128" r="3"/><circle cx="118" cy="128" r="3"/><circle cx="146" cy="128" r="3"/><circle cx="174" cy="128" r="3"/><circle cx="202" cy="128" r="3"/><circle cx="230" cy="128" r="3"/></g><path d="M90 142v50M146 142v70M202 142v50" stroke="#14BDC7" stroke-width="2" opacity=".5"/><rect x="262" y="172" width="58" height="40" rx="5" fill="#F5A623"/><text x="291" y="197" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#0B1726">UPS</text></svg></div>
          <div class="note__body">
            <p class="note__meta"><span class="note__tag">Networking</span><span><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg>2 min read</span></p>
            <h3>Why a PoE switch pays for itself</h3>
            <details class="note__more">
              <summary>Read the note<svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow" /></svg></summary>
              <p>A Power over Ethernet switch powers each phone through its network cable. Put one battery backup next to the switch and every phone stays up when the power goes out. The same switch runs paging speakers, door phones, access points and cameras without extra outlets. Phones need their own power supplies otherwise, so PoE often costs less. And because the switch is managed, we can restart every phone after an upgrade without visiting each desk.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="note" data-rv>
          <div class="note__art"><svg viewBox="0 0 380 240" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="380" height="240" fill="#0C1D30"/><path d="M110 100h40l70-46v132l-70-46h-40z" fill="#13283E" stroke="#14BDC7" stroke-width="2"/><g fill="none" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M242 100a40 40 0 0 1 0 40"/><path d="M260 82a66 66 0 0 1 0 76"/><path d="M278 64a92 92 0 0 1 0 112"/></g><text x="150" y="218" font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#14BDC7">5W IP HORN</text></svg></div>
          <div class="note__body">
            <p class="note__meta"><span class="note__tag">Paging</span><span><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg>1 min read</span></p>
            <h3>One IP paging horn vs. a whole analog setup</h3>
            <details class="note__more">
              <summary>Read the note<svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow" /></svg></summary>
              <p>IP paging horns aren't cheap. But for one horn in a warehouse, or one per zone across a few zones, a 5-watt IP horn still costs less than an analog gateway, a page adapter, an amplifier and horns. It's tidier too. If you already have a legacy paging system, or need several 70-watt horns in one spot, call us and we'll connect to what you have.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="note" data-rv>
          <div class="note__art"><svg viewBox="0 0 380 240" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="380" height="240" fill="#0C1D30"/><path d="M110 92l80-34 80 34v90l-80 34-80-34z" fill="#13283E" stroke="#14BDC7" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M110 92l80 34 80-34M190 126v90" fill="none" stroke="#14BDC7" stroke-width="2" opacity=".5"/><rect x="130" y="132" width="44" height="32" rx="3" fill="#0C1D30" stroke="#14BDC7" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="136" y="138" width="20" height="9" rx="1" fill="#14BDC7"/><circle cx="272" cy="62" r="22" fill="#F5A623"/><path d="m261 62 8 8 13-15" fill="none" stroke="#0B1726" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div>
          <div class="note__body">
            <p class="note__meta"><span class="note__tag">Phones</span><span><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg>1 min read</span></p>
            <h3>Why "cheap" phones online end up costing more</h3>
            <details class="note__more">
              <summary>Read the note<svg class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow" /></svg></summary>
              <p>Plug in an IP phone straight from an online store and it usually won't register. Someone has to update the firmware and enter your system's settings, and technicians bill $80 to $150 an hour for that. Our phones arrive upgraded and set up for your system, with a guide to the features you actually have. If one doesn't work when you plug it in, we make it work at no charge.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

